From: Daniel Martin <dmanlfc@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: wait only for our own flush bits on video mode commits

Flush bits can be left pending on a CTL for blocks outside its path (seen
on the Odin after boot), so they never latch. Waiting for the whole register to
clear then times out on every commit and caps DP on the Odin at ~8 fps.
Use the same check as the vblank irq handler.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c
@@ -538,8 +538,10 @@
 	if (!hw_ctl)
 		return 0;
 
+	/* only our own bits, stale ones outside this CTL path never latch */
 	ret = wait_event_timeout(phys_enc->pending_kickoff_wq,
-		(hw_ctl->ops.get_flush_register(hw_ctl) == 0),
+		!(hw_ctl->ops.get_flush_register(hw_ctl) &
+		  hw_ctl->ops.get_pending_flush(hw_ctl)),
 		msecs_to_jiffies(50));
 	if (ret <= 0) {
 		DPU_ERROR("vblank timeout: %x\n", hw_ctl->ops.get_flush_register(hw_ctl));
